~ю!8#ц{юA !2=~§(#ч!:=␀н°ЙJAMESON␀.elt␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Г␀А7Й␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ѓ+@␀␀E ␀␀␀␀␀␀а␀␀␀?2HSа?sа?!б?а?NElite␀я␀	Info␀©		Keys␀П	Credits@␀␀␀␀The gameP␀␀The screen‘␀␀Leavingё␀␀Flying1␀␀WeaponsЃ␀␀Jumps“␀␀ScreensV␀␀Chartsч␀␀Freeze	␀␀Saving	Ч␀␀Elite
€␀␀This versionG␀The ZX Spectrum Elite for the expanded Z88: the original Z80game code runs here, with its graphics and text redrawn forthe Z88 screen.The MENU topics have the keys.␀The game, the screen, and leaving it.␀The Spectrum keys, as in the original. LEFT SHIFT is theSpectrum's CAPS SHIFT and RIGHT SHIFT its SYMBOL SHIFT.␀Who wrote what.␀You start docked at Lave with a Cobra Mk III, 100 creditsand a pulse laser. Trade, fight pirates and police, buyequipment, and rise from Harmless to Elite in 8 galaxies. Inflight the box under the compass shows the condition: Gnothing about, A other ships about, R danger (a hostileship, or two energy banks empty).␀The map on the right holds the 3D view and the scanner, or achart. On the left are the instruments (fuel, shields,temperatures, speed, roll and dive, energy banks, missiles,compass), the view's name and the flight messages. Textscreens such as Status and Market Prices fill the wholewidth.␀INDEX suspends the game and it carries on where you left it.ESC does not quit; to end the game, KILL it from the Index.␀S and X climb and dive, N and M roll. SPACE speeds up andRIGHT SHIFT slows down. 1-4 show the front, rear, left andright views. Docked, 1 launches. - caps the frame rate: 20(default), 25, off, 12.5 or 16.7 a second, for fastemulators. = turns strict docking on (come in close to theslot's centre line, as on the BBC Micro) or off.␀A (or 0) fires the laser. T targets a missile, F fires itand U unarms it. E sets off the ECM, W the energy bomb, Qlaunches the escape pod and C switches on the dockingcomputer: each only once fitted. TAB brings an enemy in atonce (added for this version, for practice).␀Pick a system on a chart, then press H in flight: thecountdown starts and the jump follows if you have the fuel.With a galactic hyperdrive fitted, G and H together take youto the next galaxy.␀I galactic chart, O short-range chart, P data on the system,K market prices, L status, ENTER inventory. Docked: 2 buyscargo, 3 sells cargo, 4 equips the ship.␀N, M, S and X move the cursor, B puts it back on yoursystem, D gives the distance to the nearest system and Rfinds a system by name. On the short-range chart each systemhas a number; the names are listed on the left, the oneunder the cursor highlighted and a * after those within jumprange.␀LEFT SHIFT freezes the game. Then SPACE carries on and 1starts a new game. S turns the sound on and Q turns it off.B, D, R, Y and K set the Spectrum's joystick and keyboardoptions.␀Docked, RIGHT SHIFT opens the commander menu: 1 loads, 2saves, 3 goes back. A commander is saved as a file namedafter him, with .elt added (JAMESON.elt for the defaultname).␀Elite by Ian Bell and David Braben (1984). The ZX Spectrumversion by Torus, published by Firebird in 1985. This cardruns that version's Z80 code, taken from the elite-skoolkitdisassembly.␀The Z88 front end draws the 3D view, scanner, charts andinstruments natively, puts all text in OZ windows, reads thekeyboard directly in flight, and plays the game's own soundon the Z88's speaker. The Lenslok check is gone. Needs anexpanded Z88 with 48K of free RAM, and OZ 3.0 or later.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀